# C# comments

## Multi-line comments

Use block comments `/* ... */` for any comment that spans more than one line. Do not use repeated single-line `//` for the same logical comment.

```csharp
// ❌ BAD
// This validates input before
// persisting to the store.

// ✅ GOOD
/* This validates input before 
   persisting to the store. */
```

```csharp
// ❌ BAD
// Line one of explanation.
// Line two continues here.

// ✅ GOOD
/*
 * Line one of explanation.
 * Line two continues here.
 */
```

Single-line remarks may still use `//` when they fit on one line.

## XML documentation (`///`)

Use `///` summary (and related XML doc tags) **only** on **public** methods, properties, types, and other public API members that consumers see.

- **Public** API: document with `///` where a summary adds value (e.g. public methods on public types).
- **Non-public** (`internal`, `private`, `protected`, file-local, etc.): do **not** use `///`; use `//` or `/* */` as needed.

```csharp
// ✅ GOOD — public method documented
/// <summary>Computes the total for the current cart.</summary>
public decimal GetCartTotal() { ... }

// ✅ GOOD — private helper, no XML doc
private static bool IsValidSku(string sku)
{
    /* SKU must be non-empty and match warehouse format. */
    ...
}
```

Do not add `///` on private or internal members solely for consistency with public APIs.
